---
// Meet Lauren — PROTO A: "masthead profile" (Aug 28 reference: Meet Amanda
// layout — giant centered headline, small caps subline, then photo left /
// statement + small body + caps kicker right). Layout and type scale follow
// the reference; the styling stays STAND (Editorial New, cream/red, matted
// print, doodle arrow). Bio facts supplied by JY (Aug 28); the
// business-school line is lifted from the one-pager's approved copy.
---

<section class="fc-lauren" id="meet-lauren" aria-labelledby="lauren-title">
  <div class="inner">
    <header class="masthead">
      <h2 id="lauren-title" data-rv style="--rvi: 0">Meet Lauren</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="cols">
      <figure class="figure" data-rv style="--rvi: 1">
        <img
          class="photo"
          src="/brand/lauren.webp"
          alt="Lauren, founder and CEO of STAND, in front of a bookshelf"
          loading="lazy"
          width="1280"
          height="720"
        />
        <img
          class="frame"
          src="/brand/polaroid-frame.png"
          alt=""
          loading="lazy"
          width="892"
          height="1082"
        />
        <figcaption class="caption">Lauren Kassan, STAND instructor</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="copy">
        <p class="statement" data-rv style="--rvi: 2">
          &ldquo;I didn&rsquo;t go to business school.
          <em>I just did business.&rdquo;</em>
        </p>

        <p class="body" data-rv style="--rvi: 3">
          Before STAND, Lauren co-founded The Wing, a groundbreaking
          membership network built across women-focused workspaces. She led
          business development at ClassPass and was the first employee at the
          fitness brand SLT &mdash; a career of building consumer businesses
          and community-driven platforms from zero to scale.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .fc-lauren {
    background: var(--stand-cream);
    color: var(--stand-black);
  }

  .inner {
    max-width: calc(1132px + 2 * 48px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(40px, 4.5vw, 64px) 48px clamp(56px, 6.3vw, 90px);
  }

  /* Masthead: the reference's full-width display headline + tiny centered
     caps subline. Editorial New Light, much larger than the section h2s. */
  .masthead {
    text-align: center;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(56px, 8.2vw, 120px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 64px);
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: clamp(36px, 4.2vw, 64px);
  }

  /* Handwriting for the polaroid caption — proto-only face, so declared
     here rather than in tokens.css. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Mayonice';
    src: url('/fonts/Mayonice.otf') format('opentype');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  /* Polaroid: JY's actual frame asset (window punched transparent) layered
     over the photo. The photo fills the measured window (6.05/6.84% offset,
     87.22 x 72.83% of the frame) so the frame's inner bevel stays on top.
     container-type lets the caption size in cqw, tracking the frame. */
  .figure {
    position: relative;
    justify-self: center;
    width: min(100%, 400px);
    margin: 0;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.14));
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  .frame {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .photo {
    position: absolute;
    left: 6.05%;
    top: 6.84%;
    width: 87.22%;
    height: 72.83%;
    object-fit: cover;
    /* Keep Lauren (just left of frame center) and her face in the crop. */
    object-position: 47% 12%;
  }

  /* Handwritten on the chin (the frame band under the photo window). */
  .caption {
    position: absolute;
    left: 6%;
    right: 6%;
    top: 79.7%;
    height: 20.3%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: 'Mayonice', cursive;
    font-size: 4.6cqw;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--stand-black);
    transform: rotate(-2deg);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .statement {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .statement em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--stand-red);
  }

  /* The reference's small dense paragraph — a full type step down from the
     section body elsewhere on the page. */
  .body {
    margin: clamp(16px, 1.8vw, 26px) 0 0;
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    /* Same size as the Location week-table rows. */
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.4vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .inner {
      padding-left: 20px;
      padding-right: 20px;
    }

    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
    }

    .figure {
      width: min(78%, 320px);
    }

    .arrow {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
